# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LMS Swarm deployment configuration (Contabo).
#
# Copy to `.env` next to this file and fill in every CHANGE ME value:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Consumed by deploy.sh / rollback.sh (docker stack deploy interpolation)
# and by .github/workflows/lms-deploy.yml (which renders it remotely).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Domain & TLS ──
# Base DNS domain. Records needed (all → manager's public IP, or a DNS
# round-robin over manager IPs):
#   <app subdomain>.DOMAIN      frontend + API (same origin; the frontend
#                                proxies /api/v4 REST and the calls
#                                WebSocket to the backend)
#   <api subdomain>.DOMAIN      backend API (direct access)
#   <s3 subdomain>.DOMAIN       rustfs console
#   <grafana subdomain>.DOMAIN  Grafana
#   <traefik subdomain>.DOMAIN  Traefik dashboard
#
# Subdomain PREFIXES are configurable (defaults in parentheses): set any of
# them when your DNS scheme is not the classic app./api./... layout, e.g.
# under sitename.me with the lms* family:
#   APP_SUBDOMAIN=lms          (app)
#   API_SUBDOMAIN=lms-api      (api)
#   S3_SUBDOMAIN=lms-s3        (s3)
#   GRAFANA_SUBDOMAIN=lms-grafana  (grafana)
#   TRAEFIK_SUBDOMAIN=lms-traefik  (traefik)
# ⚠️ DNS must be DNS-ONLY (no proxy) for the Let's Encrypt TLS-ALPN
# challenge to reach Traefik — e.g. in Cloudflare, grey-cloud the records.
DOMAIN=example.com

# Let's Encrypt account email (certificate expiry notices).
ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# Traefik dashboard basic-auth users (htpasswd format). Generate with:
#   htpasswd -nB admin
# SINGLE-QUOTE the value: deploy.sh sources this file with bash, and the
# bcrypt hash contains $2y$10$... — unquoted, bash expands $2 as a
# positional parameter and dies ('unbound variable').
#   TRAEFIK_AUTH='admin:$2y$10$...'
TRAEFIK_AUTH='admin:CHANGE_ME'

# ── Images ──
# Registry prefix for the three application images. GHCR under the repo owner.
REGISTRY_PREFIX=ghcr.io/iamleson98
# Immutable tag for lms-server + lms-fe (the deploy pipeline passes the
# commit SHA tag, e.g. sha-1a2b3c4). `latest` works for manual deploys.
TAG=latest
# Separate tag for rtcd (pin independently if needed).
RTCD_TAG=latest

# ── PostgreSQL ──
POSTGRES_USER=mmuser
POSTGRES_DB=mattermost

# ── rustfs (S3 object storage) ──
# Credentials live entirely in Docker secrets (created by
# secrets-bootstrap.sh): the access key ID is random ("lms-<hex>") and is
# read from the rustfs_access_key secret by rustfs, rustfs-init and
# lms-server (via its entrypoint shim) — there is no env var to set here.
# Bucket for Mattermost file storage (created by the rustfs-init service).
MM_FILESETTINGS_AMAZONS3BUCKET=lms-uploads

# ── Calls (rtcd SFU) ──
# ⚠️ REQUIRED: the PUBLIC IPv4 of the node rtcd runs on (advertised in ICE
# candidates to browsers). On Contabo this is the VPS's public IP.
RTCD_ICE_HOST_OVERRIDE=203.0.113.10
# Media port (UDP + TCP, published in HOST mode on the rtcd node).
RTCD_MEDIA_PORT=8443
# STUN/TURN servers handed to BROWSERS in the join ack. Empty is the
# correct default (rtcd is on a public IP; browsers reach it directly over
# UDP and TCP). Add a TURN server when participants sit behind strict
# firewalls — credentials are embedded as URL userinfo:
#   MM_CALLSSETTINGS_ICESERVERS=stun:stun.example.net:3478,turn:turnuser:turnpass@turn.example.net:3478?transport=tcp
# (see DEPLOY.md, "Calls in production — ICE/TURN", incl. the coturn
# reference configuration).
MM_CALLSSETTINGS_ICESERVERS=
# Max participants per call (0 = unlimited). For classroom use, a cap of
# ~40 keeps call state broadcast costs sane and matches teacher reality.
MM_CALLSSETTINGS_MAXCALLPARTICIPANTS=0
# rtcd's OWN ICE servers (used for public-IP discovery when
# RTCD_ICE_HOST_OVERRIDE is empty and for its outbound gathering).
RTCD_ICE_SERVERS=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302
RTCD_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ── rtcd pool (multi-node SFU scale-out; see DEPLOY.md) ──
# The backend resolves MM_CALLSSETTINGS_RTCDSERVICEURL via DNS and keeps one
# control connection per resolved IP; new calls are spread across the pool
# and instances added later are discovered within ~10s (no backend restart).
# Default (unset): the single lms-rtcd service. Pool mode:
#   MM_CALLSSETTINGS_RTCDSERVICEURL=http://rtcd-pool:8045
# MM_CALLSSETTINGS_RTCDSERVICEURL=http://rtcd:8045
# Per-instance resource limits (raise for production video, e.g. 6.0 / 8G):
# RTCD_CPUS=2.0
# RTCD_MEM=1G
# Second SFU (label the node first: docker node update --label-add rtcd=2 N):
# RTCD2_REPLICAS=1
# RTCD2_ICE_HOST_OVERRIDE=203.0.113.11
# RTCD2_CPUS=6.0
# RTCD2_MEM=8G
# RTCD2_PLACEMENT='node.labels.rtcd == 2'


# ── Separated frontend deployment (optional) ──
# The frontend image is backend-agnostic: its server proxies /api/v4 (REST +
# WebSocket) to LMS_BACKEND_URL at RUNTIME. Keep the default when the
# frontend runs in this Swarm; when the frontend is deployed ELSEWHERE
# (another server/domain), point this at the reachable backend origin, e.g.
#   LMS_BACKEND_URL=https://api.example.com
# and set the backend CORS allowlist accordingly (see DEPLOY.md).
# LMS_BACKEND_URL=http://lms-server:8065
# Extra CORS origins the backend accepts with credentials (space-separated;
# defaults to https://app.DOMAIN). Only needed for direct cross-origin
# clients (mmctl, integrations, a frontend bypassing the proxy).
# MM_SERVICESETTINGS_ALLOWCORSFROM=https://app.example.com https://other.example.com

# ── Placement (multi-node only) ──
# Defaults keep everything on the manager — a single-node swarm works with
# no changes. For a multi-node cluster, tag nodes and override:
#   docker node update --label-add role=db <node>
#   docker node update --label-add role=video <node>
#   docker node update --label-add role=backend <node>
# ⚠️ SINGLE-QUOTE the values: deploy.sh sources this file with bash, and an
# unquoted "==" parses as a command (the var silently loses its tail).
# DB_PLACEMENT='node.labels.role == db'
# RUSTFS_PLACEMENT='node.labels.role == db'
# RTCD_PLACEMENT='node.labels.role == video'
# BACKEND_PLACEMENT='node.labels.role == backend'
# FRONTEND_PLACEMENT='node.role == worker'

# ── Scale ──
# Stateless tiers. NOTE: keep BACKEND_REPLICAS=1 — the calls control plane
# keeps per-call state in server memory and cross-node call sync is not yet
# wired (see DEPLOY.md "Capacity & scaling"). Scale the backend VERTICALLY
# (BACKEND_CPUS/MEM) and spread media across the rtcd pool instead.
# BACKEND_REPLICAS=1
# FRONTEND_REPLICAS=1
# Resource limits (match the node they run on; examples for production):
# BACKEND_CPUS=6.0
# BACKEND_MEM=6G
# FRONTEND_CPUS=2.0
# FRONTEND_MEM=1G
# DB_CPUS=6.0
# DB_MEM=12G

# ── Backend tuning ──
# Postgres pool size. ~100 for 1000 concurrent users (roughly 1 per 10).
MM_SQLSETTINGS_MAXCONNS=40
MM_LOGSETTINGS_CONSOLELEVEL=INFO

# ── Grafana ──
GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=admin

# ── Misc ──
TZ=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh
TRAEFIK_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ── GHCR pull credentials (private packages only) ──
# If the GHCR packages are private, the manager needs a PAT with
# read:packages to pull (deploy.sh reads it from GHCR_TOKEN_FILE or env):
#   echo "github_pat_..." > /opt/lms/.ghcr-token   # chmod 600
# GHCR_TOKEN_FILE=/opt/lms/.ghcr-token
# GHCR_USER=iamleson98
